# Project Conventions

- This project has no build system, no tests, and no dependencies. Do not introduce any.
- `activate.sh` must support both `curl | bash` piped execution and local clone usage — always preserve both code paths.
- Templates use `{{PLACEHOLDER}}` syntax (double curly braces, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE). Placeholders are substituted via `sed` in `activate.sh`.
- Current placeholders: `{{PROJECT_NAME}}`, `{{ROOT_FOLDERS}}`, `{{MODULE_NAME}}`.
- AI guidance files (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `GEMINI.md`) share identical content and must stay in sync when edited.
- Module TOML files go in `ai_project_index/modules/{module_name}.toml`. The TOML format uses `[meta]`, `[[component]]` arrays, `[dependencies]`, `[usage]`, `[context_loading]`, `[boundaries]`, and `[testing]` sections.
- The framework is language-agnostic — component types (`[[model]]`, `[[service]]`, etc.) adapt to the target project.
- Every line in a TOML template costs tokens across every future AI interaction — keep templates concise.
